From 05222f9b839771dd5241c7045c903e24ea402204 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Greg Anthony <5074839+gaanthony@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 09:35:50 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] pjnath: add ICE-Lite session support

Add an ICE-Lite session option that keeps the agent controlled, responds to incoming connectivity checks, forms valid and nominated pairs, and never originates ordinary or triggered checks. Preserve bounded nomination timeout behavior for silent peers.

Add in-memory coverage for peer-reflexive nomination, trickle checklist updates, early checks, role enforcement, and timeout behavior. All implementation and tests were reviewed and validated by the contributor; AI assistance was used for code drafting and review.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
(cherry picked from commit 1c6d19fd1b980fb01c0d1f2c9c9ea2353396dfad)
---
 pjnath/include/pjnath/ice_session.h |  11 ++-
 pjnath/src/pjnath/ice_session.c     | 102 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 2 files changed, 106 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

